From 0cd1a634f0fb8c642041ef3a929f0611c3de24d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:59:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(ui): draw the viewport overlay as wide anti-aliased
 lines, with MSAA

The overlay (toolpaths, height planes, outlines, triads, grid) was drawn
as wgpu lines: one hardware pixel wide, never smoothed. Each segment is
now one 32-byte instance drawn as a screen-facing quad with a one-pixel
coverage fade at the sides and the ends.

- Line width: 1, 1.5, 2 or 3 pt (default 1.5), scaled by the display's
  pixels per point.
- The ends reach half the width past their points, so two lines that
  meet close the corner and do not overlap past it.
- Each vertex is lifted toward the eye by three line widths, so a line
  that lies on a face keeps its full width in the depth test.
- Anti-aliasing: Off, 2x or 4x (default 4x). The viewport pipelines and
  the traced-stock composite rebuild for the new sample count. Only the
  counts the device offers are built; 2x needs the adapter-specific
  format feature, which bring-up now requests when the adapter has it.
- Both settings are per-user view settings (view.json), picked from the
  Theme door's new "Line width" and "Anti-aliasing" groups. They are not
  on the undo history.

The viewport pipelines and targets move to viewport/pipes.rs and the
wide line stage to viewport/wide.rs (viewport.rs: 1543 -> 1265 lines).

Fixes #2958

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
