From bdea342b62ec715a4012cfc7be39ef8d3e1f986b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:48:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(ui): line width and anti-aliasing move to the
 Display menu's Graphics group

The Theme door was the wrong place: line width and anti-aliasing are not
part of a theme. #2818 (now on main) added the viewport's Display menu
with a Graphics group, so the two settings move there, after the
projection. Like the other Display menu entries, a pick calls its State
method directly (no queued command); an anti-aliasing count the device
does not offer is a disabled entry with the reason on hover, and a pick
of one is still refused by name. The Theme door is as on main again.

The guide paragraph gets its own heading; it now says that the overlay
lines are always smooth and that anti-aliasing smooths models and stock.

Refs #2958

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
